WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.800
all right so it's time to talk&nbsp;
about everybody's favorite topic

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:15.920
oh no

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:27.200
Hey everybody and welcome to council of geeks&nbsp;
and I'm going to talk about today something that

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.960
the perspective that I'm coming at this from is&nbsp;
an lgbtq+ perspective, but I think it applies to

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.960
a lot of things outside of that. Which normally&nbsp;
is the case when I tackle these things. I have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.880
a tendency to tackle things that you can&nbsp;
extrapolate and apply what I'm saying to

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:51.200
other areas or other groups as&nbsp;
well, at least in part. So I've had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.560
this one on my to-do list for a while:&nbsp;
addressing the idea or the question of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:05.360
why is the mere inclusion of certain groups of&nbsp;
people inherently considered to be political.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.360
Now here's the funny thing about this topic...

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:16.160
I've been sitting on this for a while and&nbsp;
when I first jotted down the idea of in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.520
some way tackling this what I thought I was&nbsp;
gonna be focusing on was talking about how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:29.520
the inclusions of lgbtq+ people, disabled people,&nbsp;
neurodivergent people, racially diverse people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:33.520
is not inherently political. Why the heck&nbsp;
do people feel the need to make it that?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:44.000
But that's not where I'm going with this.&nbsp;
Because... well it IS political. But I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:51.600
there's still things for me to talk about there,&nbsp;
including covering why it is political. So first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:02:01.280
of all, something that you need to accept going in&nbsp;
is that everything has a political aspect to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.960
How much of that is intended or deliberate that&nbsp;
will vary, but there is always a political aspect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.120
to everything. It does not matter what it is, even&nbsp;
if that political aspect is simply the mindset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:17.680
and the framework, and the understanding, and&nbsp;
base assumptions, and political background, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.680
inherent biases of the people creating the piece&nbsp;
of work. Whether it be the writer, directors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.040
whatever it is. Their political background and&nbsp;
understanding that influences what they do and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.280
they come at these things, even if those political&nbsp;
views are not directly injected into the work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:42.560
Everything, EVERYTHING, that is made to be&nbsp;
consumed including art - because I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:48.960
care how artsy it is it's still intended to be&nbsp;
viewed by somebody - has a political aspect. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.960
if you are not prepared to accept that, I honestly&nbsp;
don't know how to have this conversation with you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.640
But assuming that you can go with me&nbsp;
that far, accepting that there is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:03.840
political element to everything, let's talk&nbsp;
specifically about the politics of inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:13.680
and why or at least my perspective on why (because&nbsp;
I'm not an expert) it is such a sticking point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:22.880
Especially in internet discourse and geek internet&nbsp;
discourse in particular much to my chagrin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:31.680
Well the first thing that really needs to be&nbsp;
addressed is in some ways the language. I run into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:35.920
this every now and then, that sometimes part of&nbsp;
the problem is the way that we talk about things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:41.200
And just the fact that the term "political&nbsp;
correctness" exists is part of why people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:45.200
when they see inclusion, shake a finger and&nbsp;
go "POLITICS!" Because we actually have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:51.680
word political right in the thing that we use as&nbsp;
an umbrella that this sort of thing falls under.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:55.040
Now "political correctness" was a term&nbsp;
originally coined in the 70s and originally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.720
it was much more about the specifics about HOW&nbsp;
someone was portrayed, as opposed to their mere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.040
inclusion and presence at all. But at this&nbsp;
point, especially in terms of popular use,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:10.240
it absolutely all falls under that same umbrella.&nbsp;
But I kind of want to shove that term aside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:18.240
Forget the fact that the word "politics" exists&nbsp;
in this term. That is not what makes it political,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.200
because that's just the language.&nbsp;
That's just what we use to describe it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.760
that does not inherently mean that word is&nbsp;
the best thing that we should be using or is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:34.640
indicative of exactly what it is we're dealing&nbsp;
with. But as I said at the front end, inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:43.840
is political. Acknowledging the existence of a&nbsp;
group, especially a minority or underprivileged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:51.520
or underrepresented group, is inherently a&nbsp;
political thing to do. Again, not always done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:57.040
with a political intent. But including them&nbsp;
still makes some kind of political statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:02.560
about the work, or (if you're working in a piece&nbsp;
of fiction) about the world you have created.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:07.440
I ran into this with the novel that I had my&nbsp;
kickstarter for. The Kickstarter's wrapped up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.520
at this point, but I will put announcements out&nbsp;
when the book's eventually available for pre-order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.520
and all that. I'm still working through a lot&nbsp;
of stuff, I've got a lot of things to do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.880
that. But in the process of working on that a very&nbsp;
interesting thing happened, especially once I got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:32.320
it into the hands of my editor. Now when they were&nbsp;
going over it they took note, and what was great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:37.360
was I didn't ask them to do this it's just part&nbsp;
of their process and it's actually part of why I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.960
will highly recommend them as an editor once&nbsp;
they're free and available again. Or if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.640
are now. Teresa Grabs, you know what I'll&nbsp;
put a link in the description. They're great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:53.840
but the the thing is that I very deliberately&nbsp;
made some specific choices in terms of inclusions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.840 --> 00:06:02.240
of lgbtq+ characters, or at least ones that&nbsp;
could be read that way, and wanted that to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:07.840
part of the world that I was building. That was a&nbsp;
deliberate choice with a political element by me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:15.280
What Teresa ended up pointing out&nbsp;
to me was the fact that I had failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:22.800
to include anything that indicated there was&nbsp;
disability access. Because I had a couple of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:29.040
locations where there were references to stairs&nbsp;
and no mention of ramps. Which means that without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:33.840
meaning to, simply because I didn't think about it&nbsp;
and didn't account for it, I had created a world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.640
where those specific locations (if not the society&nbsp;
and the world in general that I had depicted)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.240
doesn't make accommodations&nbsp;
for physically disabled people.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:52.480
And that has a political element because it means&nbsp;
that in the politics of this- well it meant BEFORE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:58.480
I addressed it because I actually didn't want that&nbsp;
as a background element. But what it meant at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:05.520
time of that revision they looked at, it meant&nbsp;
that I had created a world where the political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.920
choice had been made to not go out of the way&nbsp;
to accommodate these people in certain spaces.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.680
That would have been, in-universe, a&nbsp;
political decision and my failure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:22.320
account for that had political implications and&nbsp;
made inferences about the world, even though I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:27.200
didn't realize that I'd done that. Again tying&nbsp;
back to the fact that everything is political.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:34.560
So now my decision to try and amend that and&nbsp;
include some references that make it clear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:40.000
that at the very least some spaces are being&nbsp;
catered to for people with possible movement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:46.320
disabilities. That is now in there and my decision&nbsp;
to include that is political, because it means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:50.720
something in the context of the politics&nbsp;
of the world I have created for this book.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:58.720
But here's the thing I REALLY want to&nbsp;
dig into. Because it is true inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:06.320
is political, but you know what we don't talk&nbsp;
about? We don't talk about the flip side of that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:15.280
Which is the fact that a LACK of inclusion is&nbsp;
also political. Generally speaking it is framed as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:21.120
only being political when what are&nbsp;
considered to be minority groups&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:27.760
are depicted in a work. Be it film,&nbsp;
tv, video game, novel, whatever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:34.000
That is considered to be political but&nbsp;
because we don't say that same thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:39.440
about the inclusion of what is generally the&nbsp;
"default template"- and that template (in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:47.760
western culture historically and still currently)&nbsp;
is generally male, white, heterosexual, cisgender,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:54.720
and able-bodied. And we consider anything&nbsp;
that deviates on any of those five points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:59.520
or certainly if it deviates from all of them, to&nbsp;
be in a way political. But we don't talk about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:06.720
there being politics behind someone who matches&nbsp;
all five. That's taken as a given, that is taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:15.840
as being apolitical. It's not and that's my big&nbsp;
frustration with this entire framing of including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:21.120
people who aren't all five of those things is&nbsp;
in some way political. It fails to recognize the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:27.600
fact that not including them is also political.&nbsp;
That's my big frustration more than anything else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:34.720
Because I'm not going to argue anymore, I may&nbsp;
have at one point, but I'm no longer going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:42.080
argue from the position of "including people&nbsp;
of other skin tones, or body sizes, or shapes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.200
or ability levels, or sexualities, or gender&nbsp;
identities isn't political." Because it is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.440
I am however immediately gonna push&nbsp;
back and say "so is not including them."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.400
Everybody in every society has&nbsp;
their base assumptions, that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.840
why I brought up the issue of my failure to&nbsp;
account for disability in the world I created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:09.040
in my novel. Because I'm an able-bodied person.&nbsp;
I've never had to deal with physical disability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.640
and so unless I really go out of my way&nbsp;
to account for it I don't think about it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:20.080
and therefore it's not there because that&nbsp;
is my normal. That is to me the default,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:28.160
but just because it's my default doesn't rob it of&nbsp;
political implication. It's still there whether I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.800
intend it or not, whether I recognize it or not,&nbsp;
whether I fully understand the meaning of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:38.480
implications or not. They are still present, they&nbsp;
are still there. Which is another element. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:42.880
people say well "I didn't want to be political,&nbsp;
so I just made everybody a white man." If somebody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:49.440
does that, the fact that they think that makes it&nbsp;
apolitical is incredibly politically revealing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:56.960
About what they view as being normal&nbsp;
or what they view as the standard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:05.760
And your assumptions about what is normal,&nbsp;
what is standard, and what is a deviation or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:13.280
an intrusion in from that is incredibly informed&nbsp;
by your political background, your political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:20.400
understanding, your political biases, and your&nbsp;
political blind spots. Because we all have them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:28.080
Everybody has some area that is affected by&nbsp;
politics that we just don't understand, or don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:34.240
think to account for unless it's brought up by&nbsp;
somebody else. What that is will vary wildly. How&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:40.960
many blind spots people have that will also vary,&nbsp;
but we all have them. And that is why ultimately I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:45.760
am 180 degrees in the opposite direction of where&nbsp;
I thought I was going to end up on this issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:51.360
Which is not the position that I thought I would&nbsp;
be coming from, which is these "things are not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:56.800
political, stop acting as if they are."&nbsp;
No, instead "these things ARE political,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:08.160
stop acting as if their absence isn't political."&nbsp;
This ultimately is me venting a little bit at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:16.960
the discourse. Which is ultimately me howling&nbsp;
into the wind. I understand that. I am a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:23.840
small youtuber, I can't change the way&nbsp;
people are having these conversations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:30.880
And even setting aside bad actors who are going&nbsp;
to twist things for their own purposes anyways,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:35.760
even people talking in good faith I can't control&nbsp;
that conversation. But I can still put this out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:41.760
there and have it on the record: my stances on&nbsp;
these things and try to get people to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:45.520
where I'm coming from. And maybe get them to&nbsp;
think about things in a way they didn't before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:53.760
The way I've had to do with lots of things in my&nbsp;
life, not just my creative works. There are lots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.760 --> 00:13:01.120
of things I've had to have my eyes opened about,&nbsp;
to realize that my assumption that "my normal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:12.240
isn't political" is fundamentally wrong.&nbsp;
Nothing is apolitical. Deal with it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:22.000
So there you go. I don't know how much of this is&nbsp;
ultimately going to be helpful for other people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:28.320
or how much of it is just me doing this for&nbsp;
myself. But I hope you found that interesting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:34.960
thoughtful, entertaining, I don't know. Whatever&nbsp;
your thoughts are I hope you will drop something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:39.600
down in the comments and allow us to talk&nbsp;
about it. Be respectful, that is my one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:44.080
rule. I don't care what your position is,&nbsp;
if you're a jerk to me or anyone else you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:49.920
will be gone. That's how it works. I have a&nbsp;
patreon which is how this channel is able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:55.680
exist and it's how I am able to eat. It's&nbsp;
what keeps the lights on around here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.120
and in addition to that there are all the usual&nbsp;
things that you can do to help me out as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:05.440
Like, share, subscribe, and all those wonderful&nbsp;
things. Links down in the description. If you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:12.320
in need of an editor check out Teresa, they are&nbsp;
amazing, and all the other links besides for merch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:18.880
and twitters and so forth. But you also don't&nbsp;
have to, because at the end of the day you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:29.840
the council and I am only running the meetings.&nbsp;
And until next time this council is adjourned.

